LAST SHOP — STORY DEVELOPMENT: COMPLETE NARRATIVE, CAMPAIGN, MISSIONS & ENDINGS

PRIMARY OBJECTIVE

Transform Last Shop into a story-driven survival horror game with a complete, coherent, immersive, and playable main narrative.

Create and implement the actual story content, not merely a generic story framework.

Develop the narrative from the opening scene through the final chapter and multiple possible endings.

The story must be integrated with the existing gameplay systems, including:

- Open-world exploration.
- Survival.
- The shop and safehouse.
- Scavenging.
- Zombies.
- Combat.
- Survivor recruitment.
- NPC interactions.
- Missions.
- World events.
- Environmental storytelling.
- Player decisions.
- Progression.
- Save/load.

The game should feel like a survival horror story in which the player gradually uncovers the truth behind the catastrophe while struggling to survive.

IMPORTANT:

This is an existing project.

Inspect the current project, story systems, gameplay mechanics, characters, mission systems, world locations, and progression before making any changes.

Preserve existing functional features.

Adapt the story to existing mechanics instead of rebuilding the game to fit the story.

If the story system is incomplete, implement the necessary lightweight functionality using the existing architecture.

Do not merely create a document describing the story.

IMPLEMENT THE STORY AND ITS PLAYABLE CONTENT DIRECTLY INTO THE GAME.

